# Dated exceptions for the image security scan (trivy).
# The image workflow (.github/workflows/image.yml) reads this file.
# Each line is one finding id and the day its exception ends:
#   <finding id> exp:<YYYY-MM-DD>
# On that day trivy stops ignoring the finding by itself. If the finding
# is still in the image, the scan fails again.

# pillow 12.3.0: 19 findings (3 critical, 16 high). Pillow 13 fixes them.
# - Why we accept them for now: MEHO never opens image files. Pillow is in
#   the image only because the embedding library fastembed needs it, and
#   fastembed allows only Pillow below 13 (0.9.0 is its newest release).
# - Who decided: the program owner, on 2026-10-22.
# - When it ends: on 2026-11-30, by itself.
# - The real fix: Task #4729 (move to Pillow 13). Remove these lines then.
# - Only these pillow findings are listed. Every other finding still
#   fails the scan.

